% Decision-Language Model (DLM) -- THE TRUE NEAREST NEIGHBOUR (cite-and-DISTINGUISH).
% Read first-hand (docs/LIT_gap_llm_reward_optimizer.md A.5; DEEP_H2.md Sec.7). DLM is the ONLY
% prior case of an LLM that (1) proposes reward functions AS CODE and (2) iterates on them via
% SIMULATION feedback *and* (3) is shown a DISTRIBUTION -- for restless multi-armed bandits in
% public health (ARMMAN maternal care). It touches BOTH of this dissertation's axes at once, so the
% distinction must be stated precisely, NOT loosely. THE DELTAS (what THIS work does that DLM does NOT):
%   (i) OBJECT of the distribution: DLM's distribution is the spread of POPULATION GROUPS across
%       states in a resource-allocation problem; here it is the realized LOWER-TAIL of PORTFOLIO
%       RETURNS (a multi-level CVaR profile + left-tail mass + robust skew) -- a different kind of
%       distribution over a different kind of object.
%   (ii) the off-critic, 3-way DECOUPLING of fed (training-return EVT tail) / selected (tail-blind
%       validation Deflated Sharpe) / tested (sealed-leg empirical CVaR), which DLM does not isolate.
%   (iii) DOMAIN: risk-sensitive financial portfolio allocation (forcing a contamination/PIT defence),
%       not public-health resource allocation.
%   (iv) a pre-registered, identifiability-clean comparative design (single manipulated variable =
%       the feedback channel; fixed SAC agent; matched compute) vs DLM's capability demonstration.
% arXiv:2402.14807; presented at NeurIPS 2024. No on-disk PDF in the cache; coordinates
% web-verified 2026-07-02 (arXiv abs page: title/authors/NeurIPS 2024 vol. 37 confirmed).
@inproceedings{behari2024dlm,
  author    = {Behari, Nikhil and Zhang, Edwin and Zhao, Yunfan and
               Taneja, Aparna and Nagaraj, Dheeraj and Tambe, Milind},
  title     = {A Decision-Language Model {(DLM)} for Dynamic Restless
               Multi-Armed Bandit Tasks in Public Health},
  booktitle = {Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS)},
  volume    = {37},
  year      = {2024},
  note      = {arXiv:2402.14807. The nearest-neighbour (LLM authors reward code + shown a distribution), distinguished on object/domain/decoupling/design.},
}

